<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baji Rao I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1720–1740</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baji Rao I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a>, or chief minister, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state from 1720 to 1740. A brilliant cavalry commander, he led rapid campaigns that extended Maratha power deep into northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, raiding as far as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. His expansion made the Peshwa the dominant power within the Maratha Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i.jpg" alt="Baji Rao I" width="288" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bajirao_I_painting.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
